Current-Image bounded profiling follow-up:
Both retained 256 KiB one-mode payloads execute on both new Images: four inner
TAP PASS and four nonce-bound boot/shutdown PASS. Independent log analysis
requires zero overrun/commit-overrun/dropped events on all four CPUs and exactly
87 demand roots, 86 fault-in/map calls, four memslot destructions and two
invalidations per applicable flight. All these checks pass. The original
full-workload TIMEOUTs above are not changed by the small controls.

Inclusive instrumented sums, microseconds (do not add nested durations):
  function                         GCC             EvoCC
  kvm_handle_guest_abort           50140.000       177783.966
  __kvm_faultin_pfn                 17751.024        60402.096
  kvm_pgtable_stage2_map             9538.912        35349.008
  kvm_release_page_dirty            3616.128        10784.944
  kvm_free_stage2_pgd                4443.008        27447.008
  kvm_arch_flush_shadow_memslot       816.000          581.008
Demand guest execution is 0.079562 / 0.270028 seconds; the separate memslot
whole diagnostic is 0.316724992 / 1.091386 seconds. These are single traced
samples, not statistical performance or cross-run speedup evidence. Depth,
inlining and scheduling affect attribution. The gap remains distributed:
neither a single stuck call nor page-table destruction alone explains it.
Next compiler work should reduce the measured hot-path code and validate it
with isolated cases, not start another expensive full build without a cause.

Existing payloads and the 64 MiB snapshot-only scratch disk are reused; no
kernel, module, program or large disk is rebuilt for this follow-up.
